<title>JAPAN: Bangkok subway contract likely soon - Tokyo source.</title>
<headline>Bangkok subway contract likely soon - Tokyo source.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Mass Rapid Transit Authority is likely to sign a contract with an international consortium by the end of this month for a project to build Bangkok's first subway system, a Japanese construction industry source said.</p>
<p>The consortium comprises Thai construction firm Ch Karnchang Public Co Ltd, Germany's Bilfinger &amp; Berger AG, Japan's Kumagai Gumi Co Ltd and Tokyu Construction Co Ltd, also of Japan, the source said.</p>
<p>The value of the project is estimated at 24 billion baht, the source said.</p>
</text>
